ow not human subjects  weren't necessarily not everything that  bird does a human should do got to meet  the  there sir I think he's a chicken also  this study was thirty days of pure  torture which you're not gonna be able  to do to your own arms and you might  also think that surely any form of  training that lasted literally thirty  days straight solidly would have some  kind of massive impact on muscle growth  so that alone probably isn't enough  evidence for us to think that weighted  stretching is the the new holy grail of  weight training however a more recent  study has looked at the effect that  weight is stretching could have on  regular human folk and found that by  introducing a weighted stretching  protocol into calf raises they saw  significant increases in muscle  hypertrophy and muscle size though not  necessarily in terms of muscle strength  but what's actually more interested in  this case is the huge amount of  anecdotal evidence supporting weighted  stretching so our knee for instance used  two weighted stretching and if you watch  pumping iron you can see him on the  dumbbell flyes his his arm go almost all  the way back and he talks about creating  a stretch and really building more pump  that way I personally find that when I  go to the gym if I'm getting towards the  end of a set and I'm starting to feel  myself fatigued I'm starting to feel  that muscle damage then I intuitively  stretch the muscle I've been doing this  for a long time I'll ensure tively  stretch into that and even because I can  feel that it's creating the right kind  of pump there's gonna signal growth  later on so the same kind of sensation I  get from swelling the muscle through  high rep ranges which would correlate as  well it makes sense if this is something  that increases hypertrophy not  necessarily strength  so alpha Destiny also did a video on  this topic and he talked about the huge  amount of anecdotal evidence for  weighted stretching he talked in  particular 